# `/target/` with a trailing slash matches a DIRECTORY only. A worktree lane
# given CARGO_TARGET_DIR elsewhere can leave a SYMLINK named `target`, which
# slipped past this rule and was committed — and then REPLACED the real target
# directory in the main checkout on cherry-pick. Caught by
# scripts/artifact_admission_gate.sh, which is exactly why that gate exists.
/target
/target/

# Cargo.lock is TRACKED, deliberately. This workspace ships executable
# artifacts and uses immutable snapshot worktrees as RELEASE EVIDENCE, so the
# commit must determine the exact dependency graph that evidence was produced
# from. Ignoring it broke that two ways, both measured:
#
#   * a fresh snapshot worktree had no lockfile, so every gate run had to
#     re-resolve against the registry — two 30-minute strict-gate cycles were
#     lost to registry fetch timeouts that had nothing to do with the code
#     ("unable to update registry `crates-io`", 0 test suites started);
#   * a receipt naming a commit could not identify what was BUILT, because
#     two runs of that same commit were free to resolve different versions.
#
# Proven on a fresh worktree of the same commit:
#     no lockfile  + --offline -> cannot resolve
#     with lockfile+ --offline -> resolves
#
# Never edit it by hand; let cargo write it. Release-significant commands pass
# `--locked`, so a stale or missing lockfile FAILS rather than silently
# re-resolving. Nested (non-root) lockfiles stay ignored — a workspace has one.
*/Cargo.lock
*.o
*.a
*.so
*.dylib

# Compiled axon binaries (from axon build)
axon_out_*
/tmp/axon_*
# `axon build` flagship output + its manifest
/agent_task
# Build artifacts from `axon build --emit-manifest`. T48 moved the sidecar to sit
# beside the SOURCE (where `axon-vm` reads it) instead of beside the binary, so
# it now lands in the example directories rather than the repo root.
*.axmeta
# Compiled Rust library archives left in tree by build scripts
*.rlib
# Guest VM build outputs (initramfs.cpio + vmlinuz)
/dist/

# R14 mobile build outputs (`axon target build --host mobile` → out/ios/, out/android/)
/out/

# Phase-10 AST approval markers (generated by `axon ast approve`)
*.ax.approved

# R39 Slice 1: typed export of governance/specs/ — a regeneratable index derived
# from the markdown (scripts/verify_all_specs.sh --export-jsonl), not a second
# source of truth. Regenerate with:
#   bash scripts/verify_all_specs.sh --export-jsonl governance/state/specs.jsonl
/governance/state/

# Scratch / archived probe files (created during dev; rm was sandbox-denied so
# they were moved here instead)
/.archive/
tmp_*

# Editor
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
*.swo
*~

# OS
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# Claude Code per-session state (worktrees, locks)
.claude/

# Local LLM credentials / provider config (axon-ai reads .env for API keys)
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
examples/jobs/out/

# Coq compile artifacts (governance/proofs/ -- coqc leaves these next to the .v source)
*.vo
*.vok
*.vos
*.glob
.*.aux

# test artifact: sandbox_scope_fs.ax writes here to prove an IN-SCOPE write is
# still permitted (a scope that denied everything would pass the refusal asserts)
out/

# AUDIT O006: harness skip census, regenerated per test run
target/harness-skips.log

# stray probe binaries — `axon build` writes its output next to the source, so
# a probe run from inside a crate leaves a ~44MB native binary in the tree. Two
# of them (cg, vapp) reached origin/main via a `git add -A crates/`, which is
# why the rule below is a PATTERN and not two names: the next probe picks a
# different one. Extensionless executables under crates/ are never sources.
crates/*/cg
crates/*/vapp
crates/**/*.bin
/app
/ci1
/cmp
/p
/run.axjob
/run.json
docs/*.zip

# python bytecode from the Cortex experiment runners — generated, not source
__pycache__/
*.pyc
experiments/**/*.log

# A worktree lane given CARGO_TARGET_DIR=<wt>/.target swept its whole
# build directory into a commit, because only `/target` was ignored.
# Thousands of artifacts in a branch is a merge hazard, not a nit.
/.target/
.target/

# Managed-run evidence: logs, status and scope for long-running jobs.
# Retained in the project (not /tmp, which was cleared mid-run and destroyed
# a gate log) but never committed.
/.axon-runs
/.axon-runs/
